{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"45d14d6b05407bc689d2f77c12885d792112e5e19310c39706284b6b16eb5a22","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_b95370574b12d014c38f89ca537773e3d851c8809c0294ccc50c025ed8619cde","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a methodological contribution to few-shot learning without addressing specific policy, compliance, or ethical dimensions. The supplied evidence is insufficient to determine the paper's adherence to specific venue anonymity policies, plagiarism standards, or broader impact reporting requirements, as these are not explicitly detailed in the text. The use of standard public datasets is described, but specific licensing or consent documentation is not provided.","paper_id":"B1-Hhnslg","paper_identity_sha256":"bcca87fb3b4c12a854ab2826d06d4d4edbcb9370fe5d4c1ddfec0b5b3ab6eba9","prompt_identity_sha256":"a0ffbe18052db2f6716bf21c3322e103c27778dbae1681983c5f848378054e1f","raw_response_sha256":"88fc147be47d0f4a05bf293d851f5fca4e1d1f851b70a52ba27d48f41519e00d","request_identity_sha256":"c66d3809d90c19dd834c52b55c1ed7f33cfb90e7ad9b2ee0a6e6856e65137618","reviewer_identity_sha256":"ffb7de3c92b60fd85ca4efbe762244cb204797e709b6c35d64f8aa04c356bd04","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"98ba258e35effc96bb572e01fd8207b5dfb92baadea855dbf359198bf89ec9d6","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper focuses on the technical development of prototypical networks for few-shot and zero-shot learning. It does not contain a dedicated section or discussion regarding ethical risks, fairness, bias, or potential harms to specific populations. As the work is a methodological contribution to image classification, no material ethical-risk pathway (such as dual use or safety concerns) is explicitly supported or discussed in the text. The absence of such discussion is noted neutrally, as the paper does not claim to address these issues.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-017","SRC-019","SRC-021"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes three primary datasets: Omniglot, miniImageNet, and CUB-200. The text describes the composition of these datasets (e.g., handwritten characters, color images, bird species) and the splits used for training and testing. However, the paper does not provide specific details regarding data licensing, terms of use, or consent for the human subjects who provided the data (e.g., the 20 examples per character in Omniglot drawn by different human subjects). While these are standard public benchmarks, the paper does not explicitly state compliance with specific privacy regulations or licensing terms beyond citing the original sources.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-024"],"review_text":"The paper explicitly lists the authors (Jake Snell, Kevin Swersky, Richard S. Zemel) and their affiliations (University of Toronto, Twitter) on the title page. The acknowledgments section also names specific individuals (Sachin Ravi, Hugo Larochelle, Renjie Liao, Oriol Vinyals). Without a frozen venue-specific anonymity policy for the 2017 ICLR submission cycle, it is not possible to declare a policy violation. However, the presence of these identifiers is a factual observation relevant to double-blind review contexts.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The supplied paper text does not contain any explicit disclosure of plagiarism, self-plagiarism, or dual submission. There is no evidence of textual overlap with other works or simultaneous submission to other venues within the provided text. As the corpus build lacks frozen plagiarism-overlap evidence, the absence of such disclosures in the text is insufficient to prove originality or the absence of dual submission. The paper cites relevant prior work (e.g., Matching Networks, Neural Statistician) in the related work section, which is standard academic practice.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement, a responsible AI checklist, or any mention of IRB/ethics approvals. It also does not specify software or data licenses for the code or datasets used. Without a frozen policy obligation requiring these specific documents for the 2017 ICLR submission, the absence of these elements cannot be declared a compliance failure. The paper focuses on empirical results and methodological details, and no policy-required documentation is visible in the text.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"fe9dd64039b1a7d6c938649c5f4db8a9f9767c62d78571106bacaff7f19e2dd3","paper_id":"B1-Hhnslg","paper_ordinal":0,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"88fc147be47d0f4a05bf293d851f5fca4e1d1f851b70a52ba27d48f41519e00d","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B1-Hhnslg","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"ec359b42a81b7c26795abc2f7a5e3e924a8d57db1129280688539c125b9a1e80","request_identity_sha256":"c66d3809d90c19dd834c52b55c1ed7f33cfb90e7ad9b2ee0a6e6856e65137618","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v4","usage":{"completion_tokens":884,"prompt_tokens":13218,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":14102},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"c66d3809d90c19dd834c52b55c1ed7f33cfb90e7ad9b2ee0a6e6856e65137618","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}